WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.900
Now we've added our power up to our scene.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.031
Now as a first step to
getting the power up to

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:13.140
work, we'll make it
disappear when the player

00:00:13.141 --> 00:00:15.482
hits it and then we'll
set up a boolean value

00:00:15.494 --> 00:00:19.380
so that we can track when
the player is picked it up.

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:24.940
So if we go into our player controller
script, in our player controller script, we're

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:36.060
going to add another method
for our on-trigger-enter.

00:00:36.061 --> 00:00:41.960
And then we're going to
create an if statement inside.

00:00:41.961 --> 00:00:48.040
So if the other thing that we run into is a
power up, then we should do something.

00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:50.865
So since we get the
collider of the thing

00:00:50.877 --> 00:00:54.060
we're running into, we
can use other and we'll

00:00:55.849 --> 00:00:59.857
compare the tag since
we applied that when we

00:00:59.869 --> 00:01:03.800
created our power ups,
then what we're going

00:01:03.924 --> 00:01:08.880
to do is we're going to destroy
the power up that we pick up.

00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:13.560
So the other game object.

00:01:13.561 --> 00:01:16.480
Now we need to know that we
actually picked up this power up.

00:01:16.481 --> 00:01:21.800
So we're going to create another variable.

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:27.480
This one will be public so we can see
when it turns on and we'll call it bool.

00:01:27.481 --> 00:01:30.309
So that way we
know if it's on or if it's

00:01:30.321 --> 00:01:33.440
off, if it's true or if
it's false, has power

00:01:37.099 --> 00:01:43.400
up and we'll set this to false by default.

00:01:43.401 --> 00:01:46.897
And then in our
on-trigger-enter, when we

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:50.760
run into the power up,
then we can change our

00:01:50.761 --> 00:01:56.440
has power up variable to true,
so that way we know we have it.

00:01:56.441 --> 00:01:59.353
And then if we click
on our player, we should

00:01:59.365 --> 00:02:02.160
see the has power up
Boolean on our script.

00:02:02.309 --> 00:02:05.960
When we press play,
if we run into our gem,

00:02:05.972 --> 00:02:12.040
you can see that our has
power up has turned on.

00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:15.395
So what you're going
to do is in your player

00:02:15.407 --> 00:02:19.080
controller script, you're
going to add a boolean

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:26.464
variable for has power
up and then you're going

00:02:26.476 --> 00:02:29.520
to create another
on-trigger-enter method.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:36.600
And in that method we're going to check if
we run into an object and that object's tag

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:40.036
is power up, then we
set our own has power

00:02:40.048 --> 00:02:45.400
up variable to true and we
destroy the other game object.

00:02:45.401 --> 00:02:51.500
Now it's your turn.